WEBVTT

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.700
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.420
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.150
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:16.530
One year has passed since my best friend, Hoshimiya Ichigo, left Starlight Academy.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.290
In that time, a new idol school, Dream Academy, has sprung up.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.040
DreAca's idols are really popular right now.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.050
Right now, we're in the middle of a face-off concert between the two schools,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.840
and if Starlight's representative, Aoi, loses, 
Headmistress Orihime said that she would resign.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.970
DreAca's representative is the massively new idol, Otoshiro Seira-chan.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.520
Otoshiro Seira performed a Special Appeal no one had ever seen before, called a Constellation Appeal,{I can never remember how capitalization works}

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.480
and overwhelmed both us and the audience.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.480
If I can't perform a Constellation Appeal, I'll be sure to lose.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.440
But then...

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.960
What happened, Otome?

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.590
I saw! I saw!

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.370
What? Did you see a Constellation Appeal?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.740
Nope.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.750
It's me!

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.000
I'm home!

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.920
I'm home!

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.810
Did you miss me?

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.190
Ichigo?

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.570
Welcome back!

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:00.780
Welcome home!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.410
I'm home!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.540
When did you get back?

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.020
I came back just now!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:08.790
Now?

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.990
It's been so long, but it's like you were never gone!

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.920
It feels like I saw you just last week.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.300
Yeah!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.910
Ichigo-sama...

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.930
Showing up unannounced is bad for my heart.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.040
Otome, aren't you going to glomp Ichigo? {if ever there were a place for "glomp", here it would be}{it's time}

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.150
I'm fine.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.850
I was the one who discovered Ichigo-tan, so...

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.960
Ichigo-tan!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.600
I've hugged her plenty already!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.920
Saying you "discovered" her makes it sound like you found a corpse or something. {ugh}{dunno what to do, ask in irc if you still don't like it}

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.860
Kiriya-san, you're on in five.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:42.920
Okay.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:43.840
Aoi.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.370
I'll be cheering for you!

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.370
It's Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan!

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.130
Hoshimiya Ichigo?

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.940
Weren't you in America?

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.760
I'm pretty sure she was, but what what what if...

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.890
What if she came back for the face-off concert?

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.400
That would be bad bad bad!

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.680
Ichigo-chan is an amazing idol who used a Special Appeal in her very first concert!

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:14.190
Seira?

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.940
Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.940
If you're <i>do</i>, then I'm <i>re</i>.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.640
You're Otoshiro Seira-chan, right?

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.820
Nice to meet you!

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.570
So American...

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.830
I heard about your performance yesterday on the news.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.370
That new appeal you did was called a Constellation Appeal, right? {do we capitalize appeal by itself}{no}

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.010
You were so cool!

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.840
Do you think you could do a Constellation Appeal?

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:44.510
Yeah, probably.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:46.760
Seriously?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.050
That's pretty bold.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.390
Love you!

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.500
I'd like to see you try.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.640
It's not as easy as you think.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.400
Kii, lend her a Constellation Dress. {it's not the same}

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:58.780
But...

00:04:58.780 --> 00:04:59.860
Just do it.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.400
Fine.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:06.180
I'm Saegusa Kii, Seira's producer.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.290
Let's get along.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.040
Yeah.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:16.670
A Constellation Appeal is an appeal you can only perform when you're wearing a Constellation Dress.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:19.030
This Saegusa Kii girl...

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:21.420
She's really going to explain everything again...

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.590
But, but, but!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.680
Just because you're wearing a Constellation Dress doesn't mean you'll be able to do the appeal.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.300
You can only do the appeal after you max out the audience's voltage meter.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.450
Oh?

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.800
Cool!

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.430
Hey, Aoi! Can I try it?

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.940
But...

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.240
Oh, sorry.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.370
Today won't work. Maybe next time.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.380
Go ahead.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.020
I'll let you do the concert.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.560
No.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.330
I'm asking you to do it!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.880
Aoi...

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.330
I know you can do it!

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.310
I know you <i>will</i> do it!

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:03.590
Starlight Academy vs. Dream Academy: Face-off Concert.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:06.660
Starlight has changed their representative. {what is the point of announcing your person if you can change it...}

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.970
<i>Truthfully, I should have been the one to stand on that stage,</i>

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:19.150
<i>but Ichigo is the one who gives us the best chance of winning.</i>

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.730
It's been so long since I've felt like this.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.740
I don't know if I'll be able to do a Constellation Appeal,

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.610
but I'll Aikatsu with all my strength!

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.300
Oh my!

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.790
Starlight's new representative is Hoshimiya Ichigo!

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.200
Hoshimiya...

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.710
Onee-chan's back!

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:23.330
Oh my, we'll have to welcome her.{or whatever}

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.270
Onee-chan is so awesome!

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.070
Aikatsu just got really passionate. {is this the aikatsu version of "shit just got real"}

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.440
She did it.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.570
She did a Constellation Appeal.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.070
Yeah, she did.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.850
Ichigo really grew up while she was overseas.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.570
Yeah!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:21.190
What she learned in America must've been something special.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:21.830
Kiriya.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.480
I let Ichigo take the stage for me.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.230
After I heard that you'd resign if I lost...

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.710
So you overheard.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:37.340
Sorry I said it where you could hear it.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:39.720
But you know, Kiriya,

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.350
I chose you because I believed you could use a Constellation Appeal.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.840
I trust in your capabilities.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:48.610
Thanks.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.190
Face-off concert.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.690
Dream Academy's Otoshiro Seira, who performed on the first day.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.950
And Starlight Academy's Hoshimiya Ichigo, who performed today.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:03.130
They did the unimaginable and both successfully performed Constellation Appeals.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.450
Now, it's time to announce the results.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:09.210
Who was able to electrify the audience more?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.540
The result of the face-off concert is...

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.930
...a draw!

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:23.860
A draw!

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:24.970
Wow.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.200
Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.860
She's quite the girl.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.360
Welcome back, Hoshimiya.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.720
Headmistress Orihime!

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.380
Splendid performance.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:43.700
You managed to do a Constellation Appeal right after stepping off the plane.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:45.550
Thank you very much.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.270
I might just have been lucky, though.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.340
Even if it was luck,

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.910
you've given me hope.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:56.340
Hope for Starlight Academy's future.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.240
Hoshimiya, you're coming back to Starlight Academy, right? {is re-enroll/reenroll not a fucking word}{uh, I guess not?}

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.200
Yep!

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.380
Then...

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:04.330
Here.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:06.610
What's this?

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:09.150
It's an Aikatsu phone updated to use the latest technology.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.480
It's called an Aikatsu Phone Smart. {how to capitals}{yes. also sort of glad you didn't use Aikatsu Smart Phone/Smart Aikatsu Phone}

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.050
Wow!

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:15.980
And because you performed a Constellation Appeal, you'll receive a Constellation Mark.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.240
Yay!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:21.840
Let's continue our passionate idol activities tomorrow as well!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:22.990
Okay!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.990
Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.250
So you <i>did</i> manage to perform the Constellation Appeal.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.180
It just kinda happened.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.000
I still won't lose to you.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.380
If you're <i>do</i>, then I'm <i>re</i>.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.380
If you're <i>re</i>, then I'm <i>mi</i>.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.900
I'll always be a step ahead of you.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.140
No matter how high you climb.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.200
That won't stop me from climbing!

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.500
As long as I keep moving forward,

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.570
there's going to be food moving forward with me! {ersoguhronvswef}{unless she means "As long as her Aikatsu get better, her food/cooking will get better"... judgement please}

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:53.020
Why is it about food?

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.250
My food is moving forward too!

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.530
My food's pasta, by the way.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.510
A comeback! {She cameback? comebacked? retorted?}

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:00.280
She's tough.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.530
Otoshiro Seira...

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.030
Oh?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.490
I'll see you later then, Seira-chan!

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.220
Okay.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.280
Bring it on!

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.060
Width is missing! {...?}{There's no width?}

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:12.950
Width...

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.550
Width is missing?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.730
In America, when you say "width is missing",

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.130
"Haba naissu ne."

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.280
"Haba naissu ne!"

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.480
"Have a nice day!"

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.930
That's what it sounds like!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.650
"Have a nice day" is something you say to wish someone a good day.

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.680
Interesting.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:33.440
Ichigo, you too.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.220
Width...

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.010
...is missing!

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:44.310
So you're living in the old Mizuki Palace now, Otome-chan.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:45.740
Correct!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:50.240
They decided that the Starlight Queen gets to live here from now on!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.250
I renamed it the Otome Manor!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.910
Our guest of honor is here!

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.590
Welcome back!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.080
Thanks, everyone!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.510
You look low on blood.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.340
Drink up.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.470
Ichigo.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.600
I'm so happy we get to do Aikatsu together again.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:14.710
Me too.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.640
Now then...

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.550
Cheers!

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.800
To our reunition!

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.550
By the way, why did you decide to come back?

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:26.490
Was there something urgent?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:27.380
Not really.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.490
America was really fun.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.750
But after a year, I started to think that maybe it was time for me to go home.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.810
Spur of the moment!

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.360
Otome totally understands!

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.050
It's like something PowaPuri would do.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.380
What kind of Aikatsu did you do in America? {is it just me, or have they been using the word Aikatsu a lot more ever since the second season started}{what if people forgot what it was called?}

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.260
I really want to know.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:49.640
Instead of attending a school, I went around doing whatever things I could find.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.430
I joined a gospel choir at a church for a while,

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.230
and I also entered some street dancing competitions.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:58.610
So you were like a warrior roaming the countryside!

00:13:58.610 --> 00:13:59.480
Maybe!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.730
What else did you do?

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.230
Let's see...

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:06.030
I sold seaweed bentos in Manhattan...

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.030
Sorry for the wait!

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:11.580
And cleaned the Statue of Liberty!

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.560
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.580
I did all sorts of training.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.370
And I also made a new best friend.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.900
His name is Thomas.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:21.450
A-A boy?!

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:25.760
He's an orca.

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:27.290
An orca?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:27.930
Yeah.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.300
Things happened.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.510
Love you!

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:34.010
How many things need to happen for you to make friends with an orca?

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.140
So did you learn how to speak English?

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.780
Hmm, I made do somehow.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.020
For example,

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:44.760
when I want to get off a bus, I say "fried tofu"!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.690
Fried tofu?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.030
Oh, "I get off"!

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:49.780
Yeah!

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:51.540
"I get off."

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.340
It means "It's my stop". {argjuinsinf}{alt}

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.620
There are some more I know.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.550
"Bite down and gyoza."

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:57.960
"Come together!"

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.420
"Udon's yummy!"

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:00.960
"Don't mind!"

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.210
"Whoa, shumai?"

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.050
"Wash my car."

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.720
It's all food...

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:08.500
It's a miracle she could get by with just that.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.720
Ichigo doesn't need words to convey what she wants to say.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:12.950
Yeah.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.690
Good night.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.080
It was fun hearing about your travels.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.700
There're still a lot of stories I haven't told you.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:33.700
And I'm sure each and every one of them will be unbelievable.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:38.700
I wonder what Mizuki-san's doing these days. {haven't called her that in like 40 episodes}

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.200
Ichigo, I'm going to leave the school too.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.520
Until we meet again.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:51.200
When she left Starlight Academy, Mizuki announced that she'd be halting all her idol activities.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.970
No one knows what's she's up to nowadays.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:58.490
But my admiration for her hasn't changed.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.100
I want to stand on stage with her again someday.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:03.530
Me too.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:08.720
Aikatsu is going to be changing a lot soon.

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:09.740
Really?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:16.460
Designers from throughout the world have combined to form a World Designer Council.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:20.420
That's where they decide the year's theme.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.250
This year's was constellations.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.770
So that's why Constellation Appeals are a thing.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.830
We have to hurry up and learn how to do them.

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.010
Yeah.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.770
I'm also curious about Otoshiro Seira-chan.

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:32.380
Me too.

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.370
I want to know...

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.420
I want to know.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.970
About Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan. {...}

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.060
Can you do some research on Hoshimiya Ichigo?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.560
Ok-ok-okay!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.240
Good job today.

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.900
Thanks.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.630
Here's to being roommates again.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.880
Yeah.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.240
By the way, Aoi.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:09.880
Huh?

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.810
Why don't we do some research?

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.590
On Otoshiro Seira.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.010
But how?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.510
Let's infiltration! {Let's sneak in!}{nope}

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:31.230
Dream Academy is located just off the coast of the city.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.440
It's built completely on a piece of reclaimed land.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.450
Aw, they have a bridge?

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.250
Well, obviously.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:42.740
Aoi, you made it sound like it was a fortress on an island or something.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.500
Like this.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.210
How did you get<i> that</i> idea? {And where would\i1 that\i0 be?}

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.430
Sorry, I was a little too dramatic.

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:51.210
But since I brought all this stuff with us,

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.210
why don't we do it anyway? {have some fun?}

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.960
Aikatsu... Aikatsu...

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.140
Is this really Aikatsu?

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:09.010
When did you learn to infiltrate places like this?

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.820
On a mission in Washington. {I assume this is DC}

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:11.810
A mission?

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:14.780
Ichigo, what <i>didn't</i> you do in America?

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.570
You there!

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.160
Yes?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.910
What are you doing?

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.580
We're students from Starlight Academy.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:27.490
We're here on a field trip.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:29.080
Sorry.

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:32.670
If you're on a field trip, then go through the main entrance.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:34.750
We're sorry!

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:40.430
The main difference between Starlight Academy and Dream Academy

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.680
is that while Starlight only has an idol course,

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.730
DreAca has two other courses.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.500
This is the producer course.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.860
This is where the producers who produce idols are trained.{fucking redundant japanese}

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.360
And this is the designer course.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.490
It's a course that trains the next generation of brand designers.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.690
That girl there is popular both as a designer and an idol.

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:04.200
She's Kazesawa Sora-chan.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:07.450
Wow, she makes her own clothes.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.500
She's won all kinds of awards

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.460
and there's even a rumor that she's going to start her own brand soon.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:15.750
Hey.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.570
What's down there?

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:21.720
Go, go, go for it! Fight, fight, fight!

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.720
Let's, let's, go, go!

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.720
Oh! Oh! Oh!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.480
I have to finish analyzing this before Seira comes.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.520
Well, it's not like Seira needs my data to be a top idol.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.370
She's as strong as a monster...

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:38.530
No, a space monster!

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:41.620
Like one that goes "Gyaaaasu". {egioshtrognweofnvrthgwe}

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.630
Seira?

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:47.030
Did you get the data?

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:49.500
Seira, I love you!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:54.040
So this is the data on Starlight Academy.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:58.000
Yeah. Kiriya Aoi-chan and Shibuki Ran-chan are third-years.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.790
Aoi-chan, known for her love of idols, is nicknamed the "Idol Professor".

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:05.350
Ran-chan has been working in the entertainment industry since she was a little kid,

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:07.760
and is called the "Beautiful Blade".

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.020
I see.

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:14.050
By the way, they used to be in a three-person group called Soleil together.

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:17.560
And I bet you're wondering who the third person in the group was.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:19.530
And here's the answer!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.090
Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:23.970
Her family owns a bento shop.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:27.230
She's famous for having turned her rice scoop into a mic.

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:28.590
Yeah, yeah!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:31.340
Huh?

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.400
What's wrong?

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:33.350
Never mind.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.080
It's nothing.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.350
They almost saw us!

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:41.550
That sure was close.

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:46.830
I'm impressed. I didn't expect them to research their rivals that thoroughly.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:52.100
Alright! Time for today's lesson!

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.910
First is training to calm your nerves before you go on stage.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.940
Okay, ready!

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:04.440
First, try breathing with your stomach to calm yourself down.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:06.140
I'll monitor your heart rate.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:07.240
Okay.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.190
That's pretty intense.

00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:10.440
How scientific.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:15.080
Next, we'll use heavy weights to tone up your lower body.

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:16.420
Okay.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.210
Heavy weights?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.480
It'll probably be something different.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:22.170
Yeah.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.220
No way DreAca would use something so primitive.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:27.320
They use all the latest technology, after all.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.990
Aikatsu. Aikatsu. Aikatsu. Aikatsu.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:33.990
You're doing great.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.710
I'm adding a little more weight.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:38.650
The concept at least seems pretty similar...

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:40.940
How's this?

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.220
Ok-ok-okay!

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:47.230
It's easy to write, but full of personality.

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.290
I can really sense your feelings in it!

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.040
Great.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.730
Yeah, this outfit really suits you.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:57.670
It draws out your cute side.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.370
Wow!

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.960
The producer really has to take care of a lot of things.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:05.630
It sure looks difficult.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:07.200
But...

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.800
I wonder who came up with all these training methods.

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:14.390
Maybe they have an amazing teacher on their staff.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:57.740
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.900 --> 00:24:01.920
The phrases you shared with us today were "misheard English". {we can keep this, but I want a note on soramimi with a reference to Azumanga}

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:03.310
Haba naissu ne!

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:05.670
They're phrases that sound like both English and Japanese.

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:07.390
Next week, for Aikatsu...

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:09.970
Come together!

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.010
I want to know more about Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.030
Especially about her mysterious trip to America.

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:16.930
Why don't we ask her directly?

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:18.140
Hi there, welcome!

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:19.390
Huh?

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:20.580
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:21.920
Ra-ra-ra-rival!

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:23.930
Always passionate, idol activities!
